(D1 - Discrepancy 1 repro: LANGUAGE.md:4598-4599 says `end` "belongs to
 the `exit` family of keywords and remains reserved". It is not reserved -
 this compiles and prints 7 - and `End.` on its own is not an exit
 statement either; the compiler answers "Unknown function: End". The
 manual's own examples at LANGUAGE.md:302 (`Set end to 5.`) and
 LANGUAGE.md:1094 (`a point called end.`) require the compiler's behaviour,
 so the manual contradicts itself.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D1.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   7
)
a number called end is 7.
print end.
